<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> I don't really know how I would put this, so if you want to see the sandbox page just ask.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
There's a gas that when inhaled causes negative affects on the victim.<br />
*This gas slowly turns the victims into Wood.<br />
*If the wood corpse of the victim has a piece remove, the piece removed will melt into a pile of skin-like material and blood that is classified as SCP-XXXX-2<br />
*If the victim is taken to the desired area they have after inhalation, they will be free of the negative affects and mutate into SCP-XXXX-3.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> None at the moment, may have a new instance in the future.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The reason for this to stick out or to make it popular is for the following reasons:</p>
<ul>
<li>It <em>may</em> be the first SCP to be a gas that upon inhalation begins a transformation process</li>
<li>After inhalation, the situation becomes life or death, as the subject must be transported to their desired location to survive.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The last time I had posted, it ended up reaching -14 ratings, and that made me very disappointed in myself, so my goal is to make my SCP more likable.<br />
Another goal of mine is to get some help with any grammar mess-ups on my article, as well as making the article's input more eloquent.</p>

