														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835123">
									

<p>On further consideration, you should consider how on-site soldiers are pawns, researchers are rooks, some perhaps humanoid Thaumiels on site are like Knights, some powerful tech or Thaumiel objects are rooks, the site director is the king and the lead researcher on this SCP is the Queen. Characterize some of these. Then on the SCP's side, it's the King, a Keter it makes a deal with to engineer a breach is the queen, lesser SCPs are the rest, and it's a chess game.</p>
<p>Or, mechanisms around site locks/sub-systems that the SCP compromises. Perhaps a mix.</p>
<p>Another key criticism you'll face is, how is this not just a non-anomalous AI. 079 seems more anomalous because it's an advanced AI from the 70s, and it was early series. You'll need to emphasize the preternatural jump in capability of the, presumably very basic Chess-expert algo, which shouldn't have any means to bootstrap general intelligence.</p>

							</div>

								
					
